    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If I understood correctly the question, it is more about scroll animation. If that is so, then the answer is \"I don't think so\".\r\n\r\nThe scroll animation is [implemented with side effects](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c333187fcc76d7e772dac32c2a440a949fe34be4/doc/mini-animate.txt#L38-L43) meaning that window view is actually changing to achieve the visual effect. As the animation is in place, it only reacts to other scrolling keys.\r\n\r\nThis also seems like a problem similar (or exactly like) the one in #715.\r\n\r\nSo all in all, I don't think it is going to get supported.",
            "created_at": "2024-05-15T16:21:58Z",
